description:
21 speed shifting system mountain bike for youth ,adult women and men;

The double disc brake system improves braking efficiency and safety;

As it is big item during transportation, the bike arrives with 85% assembled. You need to install the front wheel, handlebar, pedals,seat and air up the tires.

Easy assembly. The set up manual and necessary tools are included in the package;

The quick release lever makes it easy and convenient to disassemble the front wheel;

Suitable for rider height of 5'5''-6'6'';

Warranty: Feel free to let us know if there is problem of the bike;

Product description

The fork and stem direction should be as the pictures shown. The front and rear disc brakes are on the left side of the bike.

Tighten the four screws as pictures shown in diagonal order.

Pedal Installation:

Remarks:

1. Identify your pedal: Check the letter on the pedal: " L " or " R ".

2.The pedal marked “R” is the right-hand pedal. Turn it clockwise to attach it to the crank.

3. The pedal marked “L” is the left-hand pedal. Turn it anticlockwise to attach it to the crank.

Note: Dmage will occur if pedals are not correctly and firmly attached.

Front wheel with quick release lever for easy assembly.
